; NDPARTA.DSF - SP11 Task 6 two-part fixture, part A (game root).
; Paired with NDPARTB.DSF (part 2, staged as GAME2.DDB + PART2\0.XMB).
; Proves the EXTERN n 4 (XPART) switch primitive, part-to-part flag and
; object carry, and the PARTn\ asset probe (via each part's own 0.XMB)
; end to end. Not part of the automated condacts.dsf suite - staged and
; run separately via tests\build-tests.ps1 -Part. Cannot be exercised by
; the implementing agent (no CSpect/emulator access) - this is the
; owner's leg.
;
; Owner leg - exact commands:
;   ./tests/build-tests.ps1 -Part
;   ./build.ps1 -Run
;
; Expected screen output, in order:
;   PA BOOT
;   (part one external text via XMESSAGE - informational only, proves
;   A's own 0.XMB staged and loads; not itself a pass/fail signal)
;   [switch to part 2 happens here - no visible marker on success]
;   PB CARRY OK
;   part two external text via PART2        <- must read EXACTLY this;
;                                               a PARTn\ probe that fell
;                                               through to the root
;                                               0.XMB by mistake reads
;                                               A's bytes at B's offset
;                                               instead - garbled text or
;                                               the wrong sentence, not
;                                               a crash
;   PB TYPE NAME: p2    <- type any 1-8 char name (e.g. p2), press ENTER
;   PB TYPE NAME: p2    <- type the SAME name again, press ENTER
;   PB SAV OK
;   [switch back to part 1 happens here - no visible marker on success]
;   PA RETURN OK
;   "Would you like another go?" (SM13) - Y or N ends the leg either way
;
; Any line ending " F" (PA SWITCH F, PB CARRY F, PB SAV F, PB SWITCH F)
; or anything other than the exact clean sentence above where "part two
; external text via PART2" belongs is a defect - stop and report it.
;
; Optional title variant: ./tests/build-tests.ps1 -Part -Title (the two
; staging blocks are independent, so combined staging works) then
; ./build.ps1 -Run. The title screen must appear once at cold boot only
; - never again at either part switch, since a switch jumps straight
; into the new part's PRO 0 and never revisits the boot/title chain.
;
; NOTE: no CLS anywhere in this fixture's PRO 0 (a deliberate departure
; from condacts.dsf's own opening-CLS idiom) - the whole point of this
; leg is a human-readable transcript of every line above, in order, on
; one screen; clearing partway through would hide the evidence.

/CTL
_

/VOC
BENCH 50 noun
KEY   51 noun
CHEST 52 noun

/STX
