/LTX
/0 "Part one arena."

/CON
/0

/OBJ
;obj  starts  weight    c w  5 4 3 2 1 0 9 8 7 6 5 4 3 2 1 0    noun   adjective
/0    0           1     _ _  _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _    BENCH  _
/1    0           1     _ _  _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _    KEY    _
/2    0           5     _ _  _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _    CHEST  _

/PRO 0
; Entry 1: first boot. Sets the two carry-proof witness flags (100,
; 101) and the boot/return marker (102), prints the boot witness, then
; attempts the switch to part 2. On success this entry never finishes -
; switch_to_part resets the stack and enters part 2's own PRO 0 fresh,
; so nothing after EXTERN 2 4 ever runs. "PA SWITCH F" and the
; fallthrough to entry 2 below run ONLY if the probe for GAME2.DDB
; failed: EXTERN is action-typed, so a failed switch just returns and
; execution continues with the next condact in THIS entry - the same
; established idiom as condacts.dsf check 44.
> _ _   EQ 102 0
        LET 100 77
        LET 101 88
        LET 102 1
        MES "PA BOOT#n"
        XMESSAGE "part one external text"
        PLACE 1 254
        EXTERN 2 4
        MES "PA SWITCH F#n"

; Entry 2: the return leg. Reached when part 2 switches back here with
; EXTERN 1 4. Flag 102 survived the whole round trip unchanged (all 256
; flags carry verbatim across a switch, in either direction), so it
; still reads 1 on this pass.
> _ _   EQ 102 1
        MES "PA RETURN OK#n"
        END
/END
